WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.039
A password alone can be guessed or stolen.

00:00:04.039 --> 00:00:08.344
Two-factor authentication adds a one-time code to the sign-in.

00:00:08.344 --> 00:00:13.408
In this video, we enable the authenticator app, email and SMS methods, set

00:00:13.408 --> 00:00:16.890
up each one, and see how users sign in with them.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:25.329
With two-factor authentication, signing in takes two steps.

00:00:25.329 --> 00:00:29.700
The user enters a username and password, then a one-time code from a

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.240
second source that only the user has.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:35.388
Orchard Core offers three methods.

00:00:35.388 --> 00:00:39.466
An authenticator app generates codes on the user's own device.

00:00:39.466 --> 00:00:43.783
The Email method sends a code to a verified email address, and the

00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:47.680
SMS method sends a text message to a verified phone number.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:52.514
An administrator turns the methods on and sets the rules for the site.

00:00:52.514 --> 00:00:57.134
Each user then sets up their own methods, and can turn two-factor authentication

00:00:57.134 --> 00:00:59.230
off, unless the site requires it.

00:01:03.442 --> 00:01:07.164
Let's open Tools, Features, and search for two-factor.

00:01:07.164 --> 00:01:09.832
There is one feature for each method:

00:01:09.832 --> 00:01:15.662
Two-Factor Authenticator App Method, Two-Factor Email Method, and Two-Factor SMS Method.

00:01:16.121 --> 00:01:20.204
Let's select the three methods and choose Bulk Actions, Enable.

00:01:20.204 --> 00:01:25.765
Orchard Core also enables the features they depend on, such as Two-Factor Authentication

00:01:25.765 --> 00:01:29.611
Services, which provides the core services of every method.

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:35.851
The Email and SMS methods send their codes through the site's email and SMS providers.

00:01:35.851 --> 00:01:41.447
Both providers are already configured on this site, and separate videos cover them.

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:51.299
Let's open Settings, Security, User Login, and select the Two-Factor Authentication tab.

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:55.611
The first group, Two-Factor Settings, holds the rules of the site.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:02:01.792
Allow users to remember client adds a Remember this device option to the code prompt.

00:02:01.792 --> 00:02:07.517
Number of recovery codes to generate sets how many recovery codes each user receives.

00:02:08.029 --> 00:02:15.035
To require two-factor authentication for some users only, select Require two-factor authentication specific

00:02:15.035 --> 00:02:16.957
roles and pick the roles.

00:02:16.957 --> 00:02:19.809
A user in any selected role must use it.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:26.484
Require two-factor authentication makes it mandatory for every user, whatever their roles.

00:02:26.484 --> 00:02:31.017
A user who has not enabled it must do so right after signing in.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:37.453
Let's clear the roles option, because Require two-factor authentication already covers every user,

00:02:37.453 --> 00:02:39.060
and save the settings.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:44.533
The same tab also holds the Email Subject and Email Body of the

00:02:44.533 --> 00:02:48.687
email code, the Message Body of the SMS code, and Show email address

00:02:48.687 --> 00:02:51.100
in the app for the authenticator app.

00:02:55.344 --> 00:02:59.634
Users manage their own two-factor authentication from the user menu.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:05.664
Let's choose Security, which opens the Two-Factor Authentication page, with a row for each method.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.893
Next to Authenticator app, let's choose Add.

00:03:08.893 --> 00:03:11.167
The page shows a QR code and a key.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:16.047
Scan the code with an authenticator app, such as Microsoft Authenticator or Google

00:03:16.047 --> 00:03:18.820
Authenticator, or type the key into the app.

00:03:19.325 --> 00:03:21.737
The app then shows a one-time code.

00:03:21.737 --> 00:03:25.325
Let's enter it in Verification code, and choose Verify.

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:31.162
Verifying the app enables two-factor authentication and generates the recovery codes.

00:03:31.162 --> 00:03:35.584
The Recovery Codes page lists them and does not show them again later,

00:03:35.584 --> 00:03:37.678
so store them in a safe place.

00:03:38.132 --> 00:03:43.027
Under Recovery options, Reset codes opens a page with a Generate Recovery Codes

00:03:43.027 --> 00:03:45.330
button, which creates another set.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:49.822
The Two-Factor Authentication page warns when only a few codes are left.

00:03:54.071 --> 00:03:55.453
Let's sign in again.

00:03:55.453 --> 00:04:00.981
After the username and password, the page asks for a verification code from the authenticator app.

00:04:01.452 --> 00:04:05.826
Remember this device lets this browser skip the code at later sign-ins.

00:04:05.826 --> 00:04:10.144
Sign in another way switches to the next method, and the recovery code

00:04:10.144 --> 00:04:11.962
link is for a lost device.

00:04:12.439 --> 00:04:15.515
Let's enter the code from the app and choose Log in.

00:04:15.515 --> 00:04:16.999
The sign-in completes.

00:04:21.224 --> 00:04:26.548
Email authentication needs no setup when the user's email address is verified:

00:04:26.548 --> 00:04:28.386
the row shows Verified.

00:04:28.386 --> 00:04:33.584
If it is not, the row offers Verify Email, which sends a verification email.

00:04:34.047 --> 00:04:40.294
With more than one method, Preferred Two-Factor Method sets the method that the sign-in offers first.

00:04:40.294 --> 00:04:43.387
Let's choose the authenticator app, and Update.

00:04:45.087 --> 00:04:49.217
At the code prompt, Sign in another way switches to the Email method.

00:04:49.703 --> 00:04:53.867
The click here link sends a one-time code to the verified email address,

00:04:53.867 --> 00:04:56.323
and a message confirms that it was sent.

00:04:56.821 --> 00:04:59.721
Let's type the code from the email and choose Log in.

00:05:01.374 --> 00:05:04.231
SMS authentication starts with a phone number.

00:05:04.231 --> 00:05:09.944
Let's choose Verify Phone Number, enter the number with its country code, and choose Request Code.

00:05:10.421 --> 00:05:13.271
The site sends a text message to that number.

00:05:13.271 --> 00:05:16.736
Let's enter the code from the message and choose Verify.

00:05:16.736 --> 00:05:19.251
SMS authentication then shows Verified.

00:05:23.469 --> 00:05:28.159
Let's sign in as Jamie, a user who has not enabled two-factor authentication.

00:05:28.159 --> 00:05:33.075
Because the site requires it, Jamie is sent to the Two-Factor Authentication page

00:05:33.075 --> 00:05:37.369
right after signing in, with a message to enable it before proceeding.

00:05:37.823 --> 00:05:41.760
Jamie's email address is verified, so Enable is available.

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:47.113
Choosing it turns on two-factor authentication and opens the Recovery Codes page.

00:05:47.573 --> 00:05:51.675
Because the site requires it, the page shows Enabled in place of a

00:05:51.675 --> 00:05:53.213
button to disable it.

00:05:57.417 --> 00:05:59.666
Let's open Access Control, Users.

00:05:59.666 --> 00:06:03.760
A user who loses access to every method and to the recovery codes

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:09.467
cannot sign in, but an administrator can turn two-factor authentication off for that account.

00:06:09.921 --> 00:06:14.494
The permission Disable two-factor authentication for any user allows it.

00:06:14.494 --> 00:06:20.122
In the Actions menu of Jamie's row, choose Disable two-factor authentication, and confirm.

00:06:20.122 --> 00:06:24.460
The account signs in without a code, and since the site requires it,

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:27.391
Jamie must enable it again after signing in.

00:06:29.391 --> 00:06:31.669
That's two-factor authentication:

00:06:31.669 --> 00:06:35.874
a one-time code from an authenticator app, email or SMS, set up by

00:06:35.874 --> 00:06:39.203
each user and required by the site when you choose.

00:06:39.203 --> 00:06:40.721
Thanks for watching.

